on-arrival: {!
Q.us_election_2020_done = 1;
Q.us_2020_roll = this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
Q.us_2020_democratic_vote = Math.round(
    (51.5 + (Q.us_2020_roll - 0.5) * 8) * 10
) / 10;
Q.us_2020_republican_vote = Math.round(
    (100 - Q.us_2020_democratic_vote) * 10
) / 10;
Q.us_2020_popular_margin = Math.round(
    (Q.us_2020_democratic_vote - Q.us_2020_republican_vote) * 10
) / 10;
Q.us_2020_battleground_roll =
    this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
Q.us_2020_democratic_tipping_margin = Math.round(
    (
        Q.us_2020_popular_margin -
        2.1 +
        (Q.us_2020_battleground_roll - 0.5) * 4
    ) * 10
) / 10;
const democraticWin = Q.us_2020_democratic_tipping_margin >= 0;
let democraticElectors = Math.round(
    269.5 + Q.us_2020_democratic_tipping_margin * 16
);
democraticElectors = Math.max(120, Math.min(418, democraticElectors));
if (democraticWin) democraticElectors = Math.max(270, democraticElectors);
else democraticElectors = Math.min(269, democraticElectors);
Q.us_2020_democratic_electors = democraticElectors;
Q.us_2020_republican_electors = 538 - democraticElectors;
Q.us_2020_popular_electoral_split =
    democraticWin != (Q.us_2020_popular_margin >= 0) ? 1 : 0;
Q.us_election_2020_winner =
    democraticWin ? "Joe Biden" : "Donald Trump";
this.game.scenes[
    "poland_foreign_events.us_election_2020"
].faceImage = democraticWin
    ? "img/poland/events/us-election-2020.webp"
    : "img/poland/events/us-election-2024.webp";
Q.us_2020_electoral_signal =
    democraticWin
        ? (
            Q.us_2020_democratic_electors + "–" +
            Q.us_2020_republican_electors + " Democratic"
        )
        : (
            Q.us_2020_republican_electors + "–" +
            Q.us_2020_democratic_electors + " Republican"
        );
Q.us_president = Q.us_election_2020_winner;
Q.us_administration =
    democraticWin ? "Democratic" : "America First";
if (democraticWin) {
    Q.us_alliance_reliability += 10;
    Q.us_rule_of_law_pressure += 8;
    Q.eu_institutional_trust += 3;
    Q.ko_relation += 2;
    Q.pis_relation -= 2;
    Q.far_right_agenda -= 1;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Biden's victory reconnects Washington, Brussels and Polish rule-of-law politics";
} else {
    Q.us_alliance_reliability -= 4;
    Q.us_rule_of_law_pressure -= 4;
    Q.us_ambassador_channel += 4;
    Q.us_defence_channel += 4;
    Q.pis_relation += 3;
    Q.far_right_agenda += 3;
    Q.eu_influence -= 2;
    if (Q.president_name == "Andrzej Duda") {
        Q.president_relation += 4;
    }
    Q.news_headline =
        "Trump's re-election strengthens PiS's bilateral American strategy";
}
!}

= November 2020 — The American election

**[+ us_election_2020_winner +] wins**, with an Electoral College result of
**[+ us_2020_electoral_signal +]** after a national vote of **[+
us_2020_democratic_vote +]% Democratic** to **[+ us_2020_republican_vote
+]% Republican**. [? if us_2020_popular_electoral_split = 1: The popular-vote
and Electoral College winners differ, leaving the new mandate disputed from
its first morning.?]

The count immediately enters Polish politics. [? if trz_inaugurated = 1: The
Trzaskowski Palace defends an institutional Atlanticism,
while the PiS government values its own White House contacts.?][? if
trz_inaugurated = 0: The Palace and PiS value their bilateral access.?] KO
treats Washington and Brussels as one democratic axis. We must reconcile
European autonomy and institutional standards with NATO and our own suspicion
of diplomacy conducted through personal channels alone.

[? if us_administration = "Democratic": A Biden administration raises the
credibility of NATO's institutional channels and increases American pressure
over courts and democratic standards. It also gives KO an ally and removes
PiS's claim to a uniquely privileged White House relationship.?]
[? if us_administration != "Democratic" and trz_inaugurated = 1: A second
Trump administration gives the PiS government a
privileged White House route. The Trzaskowski Palace keeps its institutional
Atlantic channel separate, while wider alliance commitments remain difficult
to separate from personal access and defence spending.?]
[? if us_administration != "Democratic" and trz_inaugurated = 0: A second
Trump administration keeps the government's privileged
bilateral channel open while making the reliability of wider alliance
commitments harder to separate from personal access and defence spending.?]

- @biden_front
- @biden_social
- @trump_institutions
- @trump_bilateral
- @european_insurance

@biden_front
title: Build a democratic transatlantic front around courts and NATO
subtitle: Join KO on democratic security and make PiS defend its court record abroad.
view-if: us_administration = "Democratic"
on-arrival: eu_institutional_trust += 4; constitutional_restraint += 4; us_congress_channel += 4; ko_relation += 3; pis_relation -= 4; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The Left joins a democratic transatlantic front"

We join KO in treating courts and NATO as parts of the same democratic
security. The front gives our warnings foreign weight; PiS says we have invited
Washington to referee a Polish constitutional fight.

- @poland_events_2020_11.independence_2020: Turn to Independence Day

@biden_social
title: Use the opening to build a labour and climate channel
subtitle: Build ties below the White House and keep KO from owning the opening.
view-if: us_administration = "Democratic"
on-arrival: eu_left_network += 6; labor_credibility += 3; climate_policy_pressure += 2; us_congress_channel += 3; ko_relation -= 1; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Opposition international network"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The American opening becomes a social-democratic network"

We connect unions, climate lawmakers and the European left instead of waiting
for a presidential photograph. Labour gains a transatlantic channel, and KO
cannot claim that every Democratic contact belongs to it.

- @poland_events_2020_11.independence_2020: Turn to Independence Day

@trump_institutions
title: Protect Congress, Pentagon and committee channels from White House volatility
subtitle: Treat the alliance as larger than Trump and preserve institutional access.
view-if: us_administration != "Democratic"
on-arrival: us_congress_channel += 7; us_defence_channel += 3; us_alliance_reliability += 3; constitutional_restraint += 2; pis_relation -= 1; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The Left treats the alliance as larger than Trump"

We work through Congress, committees and defence professionals rather than one
volatile White House. Atlanticists gain reassurance without forcing the party
to borrow PiS's personal channel.

- @poland_events_2020_11.independence_2020: Turn to Independence Day

@trump_bilateral
title: Accept the government's privileged bilateral route
subtitle: Secure immediate access through PiS government contacts and accept the argument inside the Left.
view-if: us_administration != "Democratic"
on-arrival: us_ambassador_channel += 5; us_defence_channel += 5; president_relation += 5 if president_name = "Andrzej Duda"; president_relation -= 1 if president_name != "Andrzej Duda"; pis_relation += 4; party_unity -= 3; progressives_dissent += 3; eu_influence -= 2; news_headline = "The Left borrows the PiS government's Trump channel"

PiS ministers open their ambassadorial and defence contacts to us. Access
arrives quickly; so does a progressive revolt against letting the government
define both Poland's American policy and our place inside it. [? if
president_name = "Rafał Trzaskowski": The Palace pointedly keeps its own
institutional Atlantic channel separate.?]

- @poland_events_2020_11.independence_2020: Turn to Independence Day

@european_insurance
title: Treat either result as an argument for a stronger European pillar
subtitle: Insure Poland through Europe while our Atlanticists warn against distance.
on-arrival: eu_influence += 5; eu_institutional_trust += 3; us_ambassador_channel -= 2; left_atlanticist_dissent += 4; news_headline = "The American election accelerates Poland's European insurance policy"

We ask EU institutions and member governments to make Europe capable of acting
when Washington turns inward. The policy creates insurance and influence; our
Atlanticists hear an excuse to weaken the alliance that still protects Poland.

- @poland_events_2020_11.independence_2020: Turn to Independence Day

