= November 2024 — America votes, Poland recalculates

[? if us_2024_republican_candidate = "Donald Trump": President **Joe Biden's**
withdrawal leaves Vice-President **Kamala Harris**, the Democratic nominee,
opposite former president **Donald Trump**, returning for the Republicans. The
contest offers Poland no neutral result: it is also a vote on NATO, Ukraine
and whether personal access can substitute for an alliance.?]
[? if us_2024_republican_candidate != "Donald Trump": President **Donald
Trump** cannot seek a third term in this timeline. **Nikki Haley**, **Ron
DeSantis**, **Marco Rubio**, **JD Vance** and **Vivek Ramaswamy** represented
rival claims to his inheritance; the five camps fought through the primaries
until **[+ us_2024_republican_candidate +]** emerged to inherit the America
First machine. Democrats nominate **Kamala Harris** against the Republican
nominee.?]

The television map settles it: **[+ us_election_2024_winner +] wins**, with an
Electoral College result of **[+ us_2024_electoral_signal +]**. The national
vote is **[+ us_2024_republican_vote +]% Republican** to **[+
us_2024_democratic_vote +]% Democratic**.[? if
us_2024_popular_electoral_split = 1: Once again, the popular vote and the
electors point in different directions, and every Polish faction can choose
the mandate it prefers to see.?]

[? if us_election_2024_winner = "Donald Trump": Before dawn, **Jarosław
Kaczyński** says PiS understands the returning president; **Donald Tusk's** KO
answers that only an institutional Atlantic alliance can survive him. Both
claims threaten to reduce Lewica to an adjective in somebody else's foreign
policy. The party must choose between European insurance, durable American
institutions and an expensive accommodation through the Palace.?]
[? if us_2024_republican_candidate != "Donald Trump" and us_election_2024_winner
!= "Kamala Harris": **[+ us_election_2024_winner +]** inherits Trump's demands
for spending, bases and loyalty, but not his personal bond with Polish
conservatives. PiS still promises privileged access and KO still promises
Atlantic repair. Lewica has a narrow opening to define security on its own
terms before either story hardens.?]
[? if us_election_2024_winner = "Kamala Harris": Harris restores a predictable
institutional channel and puts democratic standards back beside NATO policy.
That is welcome terrain for Lewica, but it is also Tusk's easiest terrain: if
the Left merely applauds, KO will own both the photograph and the argument.
The choice is whether to join that front or give the opening a distinct social
and security content.?]

- @gop_europe
- @gop_channels
- @gop_bilateral
- @harris_security
- @harris_rules
- @harris_social

@gop_europe
title: Build the EU pillar into Poland's first insurance policy
subtitle: Make European institutions and Ukraine policy carry more of the burden, while Polish Atlanticists call it a retreat.
view-if: us_administration != "Democratic"
on-arrival: eu_influence += 7; eu_institutional_trust += 5; ukraine_solidarity += 4; us_ambassador_channel -= 3; us_defence_channel -= 1; left_atlanticist_dissent += 4; news_headline = "The EU becomes Poland's insurance against Washington"

We refuse to buy calm from President-elect **[+ us_election_2024_winner +]**
one bilateral favour at a time. Lewica's delegations go instead through EU
institutions and governments that cannot afford an American withdrawal from
Ukraine. They agree to keep European
capacity on the table; Washington's ambassador notices the empty chair, and
our Atlanticists accuse the leadership of turning insurance into distance.

- @poland_event_queue: Go through Brussels

@gop_channels
title: Ring-fence Congress, defence and intelligence cooperation
subtitle: Treat the alliance as larger than its president, knowing the White House can still punish those who go around it.
view-if: us_administration != "Democratic"
on-arrival: us_congress_channel += 8; us_defence_channel += 5; us_alliance_reliability += 4; constitutional_restraint += 2; news_headline = "Institutional channels contain the American election shock"

Lewica MPs begin with committees, congressional staff and the professionals
who keep allied planning alive between elections. The message is deliberately
unromantic: Poland will meet its obligations, scrutinise procurement and keep
Ukraine policy in institutions no president owns alone. The White House gives
us no photograph, but the working channels remain open—and PiS loses its claim
that access to one man is the same thing as access to America.

- @poland_event_queue: Ring-fence the channels

@gop_bilateral
title: Seek a direct spending-and-basing guarantee
subtitle: Borrow the Palace's access and pay for reassurance in money, European influence and a fight inside Lewica.
view-if: us_administration != "Democratic"
on-arrival: us_defence_channel += 8; us_ambassador_channel += 6; president_relation += 4; pis_relation += 4; fiscal_stress += 6; party_unity -= 4; eu_influence -= 3; news_headline = "A bilateral guarantee arrives with a domestic and European price"

President **[+ president_name +]** places the Palace's contacts at our disposal.
The answer from the incoming administration is a political guarantee of
continued basing talks and defence access, tied to a larger Polish spending
commitment; it is not a treaty and the Sejm has appropriated nothing yet. PiS
welcomes Lewica into the bilateral camp. Our Europeanists and social wing hear
only the programmes that will be squeezed to pay the entrance fee.

- @poland_event_queue: Seek the guarantee

@harris_security
title: Offer Harris a parliamentary compact for Ukraine, NATO and civil resilience
subtitle: Commit Lewica's votes and credibility to durable support, including the bill that comes with it.
view-if: us_administration = "Democratic"
on-arrival: us_alliance_reliability += 5; us_defence_channel += 5; military_trust += 4; ukraine_solidarity += 4; eu_influence += 3; fiscal_stress += 2; news_headline = "The incoming administration receives a Polish security compact"

The paper delivered to Harris's transition team promises no ministerial order
Lewica does not control. It offers something the party can give: votes for
durable Ukraine support, scrutiny of NATO commitments, and a civil-resilience
programme linking shelters, railways and hospitals to national security. The
military establishment welcomes the continuity. The party's social wing asks,
correctly, what will be postponed to fund it.

- @poland_event_queue: Offer the compact

@harris_rules
title: Join the democratic-institutions front and publish Polish red lines
subtitle: Stand beside KO on courts and constitutional rules, then fight over who owns the democratic victory.
view-if: us_administration = "Democratic"
on-arrival: us_rule_of_law_pressure += 3; eu_institutional_trust += 5; constitutional_restraint += 4; ko_relation += 3; pis_relation -= 5; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The American result reinforces Poland's rule-of-law argument"

Lewica and KO publish one set of red lines: military cooperation cannot be a
reward for dismantling courts, and democratic allies may criticise one
another without becoming foreign masters. **Donald Tusk** welcomes the common
front; **Jarosław Kaczyński** calls it an invitation for Washington to govern
Poland. The front is credible abroad. At home, Lewica must now work to ensure
that voters remember more than Tusk standing at its centre.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the red lines

@harris_social
title: Prevent KO owning the result through a labour and climate partnership
subtitle: Go below the summit—to unions, climate legislators and cities—and give the Atlantic opening a Left programme.
view-if: us_administration = "Democratic"
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 4; eu_left_network += 6; climate_policy_pressure += 3; workers_support += 2; ko_relation -= 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.2; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Opposition international network"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The Left gives the Atlantic opening a social programme"

While KO competes for the first White House photograph, Lewica opens a lower
and wider door. A party delegation meets **Liz Shuler** of the AFL–CIO and
**Pramila Jayapal's** congressional progressives, joining industrial wages to
the climate transition instead of treating them as rival causes. No Polish law
changes in Washington. A network does, and KO discovers that friendship with a
Democratic administration need not belong to liberals alone.

- @poland_event_queue: Build the labour channel

@hungary_election_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — The model no longer narrates its own roll; the result is Hungary's, stated plainly to a Warsaw about to read it as a verdict on itself. Both outcomes are researched to the seat, and change, survival and state-level correctness each end in a consequence Lewica has to live with.
