- @poland_event_queue: Use the Palace channel

@review_parliament
title: Put Congress and the Sejm committees at the centre
subtitle: Build a relationship that can survive presidents, at the cost of the single Polish voice Washington requested.
on-arrival: us_congress_channel += 7; constitutional_restraint += 3; party_unity += 2; left_atlanticist_dissent -= 2; media_capacity += 1; news_headline = "Parliamentary diplomacy widens the American relationship"

Lewica answers an executive review with legislators. Sejm committees publish
their questions, our MPs open a permanent line to Congress, and defence
professionals brief both sides in rooms without presidential flags. The
American delegation does not get the single command chain it requested. It
does get a relationship capable of surviving **[+ us_president +]**, **[+
president_name +]** and the next election in either country.

- @poland_event_queue: Take it to the committees

@review_europe
title: Answer through the completed European programme
subtitle: Meet American leverage with allies already assembled in Europe, even if Washington reads self-reliance as distance.
choose-if: eu_campaign_complete = 1 or eu_influence >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: Poland has not built enough European leverage for this answer.
on-arrival: eu_influence += 5; eu_institutional_trust += 4; ukraine_solidarity += 3; us_alliance_reliability -= 1; us_ambassador_channel -= 2; foreign_pressure -= 2; news_headline = "The Polish EU settlement becomes Poland's answer to Washington"

We place the completed Polish EU programme on the table: democratic law,
social investment, Ukraine and a European capacity that does not disappear when
the White House changes hands. President **[+ us_president +]** receives a
Poland able to bargain rather than plead. The price is a colder ambassadorial
channel and a fresh suspicion in Washington that European insurance is being
prepared for use against its insurer.

- @poland_event_queue: Answer through Europe
